  "Question": "The parabola \\(y = ax^2 + bx + c\\) has vertex \\((p, p)\\) and \\(y\\)-intercept \\((0, -p),\\) where \\(p \\neq 0.\\) What is \\(b?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-p\\)",
    "B": "\\(0\\)",
    "C": "\\(2\\)",
    "D": "\\(4\\)",
    "E": "\\(p\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The given vertex makes vertex form useful: it incorporates both vertex coordinates immediately. Since the vertex is \\((p,p)\\), write\n\\[\ny=a(x-p)^2+p,\n\\]\nwhere \\(a\\ne0\\) because the graph is a parabola. At the \\(y\\)-intercept, \\(x=0\\) and \\(y=-p\\), so\n\\[\nap^2+p=-p,\n\\qquad ap^2=-2p.\n\\]\nBecause \\(p\\ne0\\), division by \\(p\\) gives \\(ap=-2\\).\n\nExpanding the vertex form gives\n\\[\ny=ax^2-2apx+ap^2+p.\n\\]\nThe coefficient of \\(x\\) is therefore\n\\[\nb=-2ap=-2(-2)=\\boxed{4},\n\\]\nchoice (D).",
